{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3f7d9a1e-ecoserve-2026-step97",
    "name": "ECOSERVE API — Phase 38 Step 97",
    "description": "API test suite for the Ecoserve food-redistribution platform.\n\nRun the folders in order so chained variables (tokens, donationId, deliveryId, ...) are captured:\n\n  1. Setup — Supabase auth (signup once, then login each run)\n  2. Auth & Sessions (backend register + token lifecycle)\n  3. Donation\n  4. NGO\n  5. Volunteer\n  6. Assignment\n  7. Delivery\n  8. Analytics\n  9. Admin\n  10. Notifications\n\nAuth model: the frontend authenticates directly against Supabase (GoTrue) and\npresents the access token to the backend. Every backend request below sends\n`Authorization: Bearer <role-token>`, captured from the Supabase login/signup\nresponses into collection variables.\n\nAdmin note: ADMIN accounts cannot be self-registered (roles are DONOR | NGO |\nVOLUNTEER). Create an admin user in the Supabase dashboard and set its role to\nADMIN in the users table (see docs/postman/README.md) before using the Admin folder.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 · Setup — Supabase auth",
      "item": [
